<report>
<title>One way analysis of variance</title>

<p>Variables: @tlist</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Source of Variation</th><th>Sum Squares</th><th>DF</th><th>Mean Square</th></tr>
<tr><td>Between Groups</td><td>@{b_sum:roundu}</td><td>@b_df</td><td>@{b_mean:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Within Groups</td><td>@{w_sum:roundu}</td><td>@w_df</td><td>@{w_mean:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Corrected Total</td><td>@{t_sum:roundu}</td><td>@t_df</td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<p>F (variance ratio) = @{f:roundu}  <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>
</report>
